nt plan is in place and an installment is missed, it also creates a financial hold.\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": \"An unpaid balance receives a USD 75 late-payment fee and a financial hold. The hold blocks new registration, official transcripts, and graduation clearance.\", \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"What fees and holds result from an unpaid financial balance?\", \"retrieval_context\": null}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Answer Relevancy", "threshold": 0.5, "success": false, "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "gpt-4o-mini", "evaluationCost": 0, "inputTokenCount": 0, "outputTokenCount": 0}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.5, "evaluation_model": "gpt-4o-mini", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}]}, "{\"actual_output\": \"An incomplete grade `I` may be granted under the following conditions: at least 70% of assessed work is complete, the student was passing before an unexpected documented event, and the remaining work can be completed independently. Both the student and instructor must sign an incomplete plan, with a default deadline for completion set at the end of the next regular term. If no grade is submitted by that deadline, the `I` converts to `F` unless an approved extension exists.\\n\\nAcademic disagreements are first addressed with the instructor. If the issue involves alleged calculation errors, procedural unfairness, discrimination, or inconsistency with the published syllabus, it may proceed to a formal grade appeal. A student must request clarification from the instructor within five business days after the final grade is published and file a formal appeal within ten business days, identifying at least one permitted ground. Disagreement with academic judgment alone is not a valid ground for appeal.\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": \"An incomplete grade I requires at least 70% of assessed work complete and passing status before an unexpected event. Disagreements on academic judgement are handled first with the instructor and can proceed to grade appeals for procedural or calculation errors.\", \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"What conditions allow an incomplete grade I, and how are academic disagreements handled?\", \"retrieval_context\": null}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Answer Relevancy", "threshold": 0.5, "success": false, "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "gpt-4o-mini", "evaluationCost": 0, "inputTokenCount": 0, "outputTokenCount": 0}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.5, "evaluation_model": "gpt-4o-mini", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}]}}}